# GitList 0.4.0 argument-injection RCE (no creds) -> credentials committed in
# the repository history -> proper login for the account's flag (the mail
# sits in a file in its home directory) -> sudo apt-get -> root. The root
# payload names "Cryptography Lab terminal 03" and 00:47:00; every in-game
# reference to the terminal uses that name. The login name is random per
# build, so no game text names the account. SecGen system_name for the
# target is `safetynet_gitlist_server`. Four flags; the fallback strings below are placeholders
# for standalone/dev render -- the real per-build flags arrive via vm_context in
# Hacktivity mode. FLAG ORDER against flags_by_vm['safetynet_gitlist_server'] STILL NEEDS
# VERIFICATION against a real build (see PASS2_IMPROVEMENTS.md, "Unverified").
#
# ROOM LAYOUT (grid units; door sides verified by predict_door_sides.py):
#
# (PASS 3: redrawn to match the connections below; the old drawing put
#  Intel Analysis over the Crypto Lab and the Director's Office south.)
#
#                          [Director's Office]   [Intel Analysis]
#                                  |                    |
#   [Break Room]--[Crypto Lab]--[Main Lobby]------[Ops Floor]--[Server Room] (rfid)
#                      |                                |
#           [Interrogation] (pin)          [Security Archives] (password)
#
#   Connections (all reciprocal):
#     main_lobby        N director_office  E operations_floor  W cryptography_lab
#     operations_floor  N intel_analysis   E server_room       S security_archives
#     cryptography_lab  S interrogation_room  W break_room
#
# LOCK CHAIN (PASS 3; see PUZZLE_CHAINS_PLAN.md):
#   rfid     server_room        <- Director Netherton's keycard, CLONED off his lanyard with the
#                                  start-kit RFID cloner once all three suspects are interviewed
#                                  (PASS 4), or the card itself dropped on a KO
#                                  | badge printer (lobby, PIN on the break-room post-it): the
#                                  earned early route
#   password security_archives  <- post-it in the break room only (ATHENA hints, never reads it)
#   pin      director_safe      <- the Director's service number, printed as "requested by"
#                                  on the ops-floor personnel printout
#   pin      interrogation_room <- suite_code: the code card in director_safe, or Netherton
#                                  aloud after a correct reading of the door audit (P6).
#                                  Picks can't open it; the PIN cracker isn't in the kit.
#   key      vector_locker / nightshade_locker / phantom_locker (break room, 0x23 / 0x47 / 0x88)
